{"id": "EUVD-2026-87055", "enisaUuid": "38816c93-17e5-391c-ab79-6ac4bf9322f1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/srpt: Fix srpt_alloc_rw_ctxs() unwind counters\n\nWhen srpt_alloc_rw_ctxs() fails partway through a multi-buffer indirect\ndescriptor, the unwind path destroys RDMA contexts but leaves stale\nn_rw_ctx and n_rdma values (and a dangling rw_ctxs pointer). Later\nsq_wr_avail accounting in srpt_queue_response() or srpt_write_pending()\ncan then subtract the wrong number of send queue credits.\n\nReset the counters and clear rw_ctxs after freeing the heap\nallocation before returning an error.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T13:06:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:43:07", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af00051dbc9f467d4840ec709680660a3f8990fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/717ab4d0614e9446bf8e2de6229464499e4008d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f1f2252da52cdda912da9993f39f58783b01b38f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f65f45dfa1e6e2eaa9e11c8b8ce8857799cb189d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be1478849e1abb1e12dc12e14cdbf800cc6fa99a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af073bd245180393bcb15d33d3990a6bdc32593a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd02d644bd19a2795c018635d273d91e45d2bb95", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b38f98e176050850f41bb6415f3a71400056623e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6wcw-wcgc-6j9r", "CVE-2026-100075"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14e629b7-6563-3e8c-b17d-74c2c56d45b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b99f8e4d7bcd3bfbb3cd965918523299370d0cb2 <717ab4d0614e9446bf8e2de6229464499e4008d6"}, {"id": "15c2b090-e412-331f-94a9-16eb8c850797", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b99f8e4d7bcd3bfbb3cd965918523299370d0cb2 <f1f2252da52cdda912da9993f39f587